color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Battles will enter with double the normal number of defense counters.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Doubling Season affects permanents that enter with counters.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Everything that is specified by the effect creating the original token or tokens will also be true about the additional token or tokens created by Doubling Season's replacement effect. For example, if an effect tells you to create a token \"tapped and attacking,\" the additional tokens will also be tapped and attacking.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If there are two Doubling Seasons on the battlefield, then the number of tokens or counters is four times the original number. If there are three on the battlefield, then the number of tokens or counters is eight times the original number, and so on.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Planeswalkers will enter with double the normal number of loyalty counters. However, if you activate an ability whose cost has you put loyalty counters on a planeswalker, the number you put on isn't doubled. This is because those counters are put on as a cost, not as an effect.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the copied spell divides damage or distributes counters among a number of targets, the division and number of targets can’t be changed. If you choose new targets, you must choose the same number of targets.","oracle_id":"b3a80545-9a8a-46b2-9d8c-b0d66fb68a5d","published_at":"2024-04-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell that’s copied has an X whose value was determined as it was cast, the copy will have the same value of X.","oracle_id":"b3a80545-9a8a-46b2-9d8c-b0d66fb68a5d","published_at":"2024-04-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell that’s copied is modal (that is, it says “Choose one —” or the like), the copy will have the same mode or modes. You can’t choose different ones.","oracle_id":"b3a80545-9a8a-46b2-9d8c-b0d66fb68a5d","published_at":"2024-04-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Protection from instants and from sorceries means that the equipped creature can’t be the target of instant spells, sorcery spells, or abilities from instant or sorcery cards (such as an ability of an instant card that triggers when that card is cycled), and all damage that an instant or sorcery spell or card would deal to it is prevented. Nothing other than these events is prevented or illegal.","oracle_id":"b3a80545-9a8a-46b2-9d8c-b0d66fb68a5d","published_at":"2024-04-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copy created by Sword of Wealth and Power’s delayed triggered ability will have the same targets as the spell it’s copying unless you choose new ones. You may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. The new targets must be legal.","oracle_id":"b3a80545-9a8a-46b2-9d8c-b0d66fb68a5d","published_at":"2024-04-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copy made by Sword of Wealth and Power’s delayed triggered ability is created on the stack, so it’s not “cast.”","oracle_id":"b3a80545-9a8a-46b2-9d8c-b0d66fb68a5d","published_at":"2024-04-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can’t choose to pay any additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy too.","oracle_id":"b3a80545-9a8a-46b2-9d8c-b0d66fb68a5d","published_at":"2024-04-12","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
